---
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400.css';
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/500.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/600.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css';
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import FreshnessTimeline from '../../../components/coffee/FreshnessTimeline.svelte';
import { freshnessStages, SOURCES } from '../../../lib/coffee/index.ts';

const title = 'Coffee Freshness: How Long Do Coffee Beans Last?';
const description = 'Enter the roast date from the bag and see where your beans are: still resting, at their peak, or fading. Peak dates, storage and freezing advice for filter and espresso.';
const filter = freshnessStages('filter');
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			'@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'Coffee Freshness Tracker', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee/tools/freshness/', description,
			applicationCategory: 'UtilityApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'JayArr Coffee', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee' },
		})}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="cf-page">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="cf-intro">
				<a href="/tools/" class="cf-back">← All tools</a>
				<p class="cf-kicker">Freshness</p>
				<h1>How fresh are <em>your beans?</em></h1>
				<p class="cf-lede">Enter the roast date printed on the bag. You'll see whether the coffee is still resting, at its peak or fading, and the dates of its best window.</p>
			</section>
			<section class="cf-tool" aria-label="Freshness tracker"><FreshnessTimeline client:load /></section>

			<article class="cf-body">
				<h2>How long do coffee beans last?</h2>
				<p>Whole beans taste best roughly one to three weeks after roasting, and are worth finishing within about a month. James Hoffmann's rule of thumb is to buy within two weeks of the roast date and use within a month. After that they don't go bad, but the aroma fades and cups turn flat.</p>
				<div class="cf-table-wrap">
					<table>
						<thead><tr><th scope="col">Days since roast</th><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">What to do</th></tr></thead>
						<tbody>
							{filter.map((s) => <tr><td>{s.to === Infinity ? `${s.from}+` : `${s.from}–${s.to - 1}`}</td><th scope="row">{s.label}</th><td>{s.advice}</td></tr>)}
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
				<p class="cf-note">Filter coffee timings. For espresso, give the beans a few more days of rest; the extra CO₂ in very fresh beans makes shots run unevenly. The boundaries after a month are our guide, not a rule.</p>

				<h2>Why fresh beans need a rest</h2>
				<p>Roasting fills the beans with carbon dioxide. In the first few days it bubbles out so fast that it pushes water away from the grounds and makes extraction uneven, so a coffee roasted yesterday can taste sharp and thin. A few days' rest lets it settle; after that, aroma compounds slowly escape and oils oxidize, which is why beans peak and then fade. Fresh beans don't look oily; very oily beans are often old or very dark.</p>

				<h2>How to store coffee</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Keep it sealed, cool, dark and dry.</strong> The original bag with the air squeezed out is fine.</li>
					<li><strong>Never the fridge:</strong> beans pick up smells and moisture condenses on them.</li>
					<li><strong>Freeze what you won't use in two weeks.</strong> Sealed and frozen, beans keep for months; take out only what you need and don't refreeze.</li>
					<li><strong>Grind close to brewing.</strong> Ground coffee loses aroma much faster than whole beans, though grinding a batch for drip a few hours ahead is fine.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Related guides</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="/blog/coffee-freshness-roast-to-stale/">Coffee freshness from roast to stale</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/how-to-store-coffee-beans/">How to store coffee beans</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/how-to-freeze-coffee-beans/">How to freeze coffee beans</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/bean-resting-for-espresso-freshness-trap/">Resting beans for espresso</a></li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Sources</h2>
				<ul class="cf-sources">
					{['gagne', 'rao', 'hoffmann', 'synthesis'].map((id) => SOURCES[id]).map((s) => <li>{s.author}, <cite>{s.title}</cite>{s.year ? ` (${s.year})` : ''}.</li>)}
				</ul>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>.cf-page { background: #f3ede3; }</style>
<style>
	main { color: #2a1d15; }
	.cf-intro { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 22px; }
	.cf-back { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; text-decoration: none; }
	.cf-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8f5d22; margin: 26px 0 0; }
	h1 { font: 400 clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px)/.98 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 10px 0 12px; }
	h1 em { font-style: italic; color: #7a4e30; }
	.cf-lede { font: 400 17px/1.5 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #5b4a3d; max-width: 60ch; margin: 0; }
	.cf-tool { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8px 24px 40px; }
	.cf-body { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 24px 72px; font: 400 17px/1.7 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; }
	.cf-body h2 { font: 400 34px/1.1 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; margin: 44px 0 12px; }
	.cf-body a { color: #7a4e30; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
	.cf-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid #d9cdbd; border-radius: 12px; background: #fbf8f3; }
	table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 15px; }
	th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e6dccd; vertical-align: top; }
	thead th { font: 500 11px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; }
	td:first-child { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; white-space: nowrap; }
	tr:last-child th, tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
	.cf-note, .cf-sources { font-size: 14.5px; color: #5b4a3d; }
	@media (max-width: 640px) { .cf-intro { padding: 96px 16px 18px; } .cf-tool { padding: 4px 12px 32px; } .cf-body { padding: 16px 16px 56px; } }
</style>
